      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.088,
            0.763,
            0.108
          ],
          "content": "3. What will be the digital root of the number 9a + 36b + 13?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.114,
            0.507,
            0.153
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.** 9a $\\begin{aligned}+ 36b + 13 &= 9a + 36b + 9 + 4 \\\\&= 9(a + 4b + 1) + 4\\end{aligned}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.201,
            0.155,
            0.5,
            0.173
          ],
          "content": "9 (a + 4b + 1) is a multiple of 9."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.201,
            0.174,
            0.669,
            0.194
          ],
          "content": "The digital root of any multiple of 9 is always 9."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.201,
            0.194,
            0.744,
            0.213
          ],
          "content": "So, Digital root of 9 (a + 4b + 1) + 4 will be 9 + 4 = 13 → 4"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.224,
            0.847,
            0.261
          ],
          "content": "4. Make conjectures by examining if there are any patterns or relations between"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.214,
            0.267,
            0.669,
            0.286
          ],
          "content": "(i) the parity of a number and its digital root."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.29,
            0.846,
            0.328
          ],
          "content": "(ii) the digital root of a number and the remainder obtained when the number is divided by 3 or 9."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.337,
            0.204,
            0.353
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Ans."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.214,
            0.354,
            0.847,
            0.391
          ],
          "content": "(i) There is no consistent pattern between the parity of a number and its digital root."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.395,
            0.846,
            0.434
          ],
          "content": "(ii) (a) If the digital root of a number is 1, 4, 7, then the remainder obtained after dividing the number by 3 will be 1."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.284,
            0.438,
            0.847,
            0.477
          ],
          "content": "If the digital root of a number is 2, 5, 8, then the remainder obtained after dividing the number by 3 will be 2."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.284,
            0.48,
            0.847,
            0.519
          ],
          "content": "If the digital root of a number is 3, 6, 9, then the remainder obtained after dividing the number by 3 will be 0."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.258,
            0.525,
            0.848,
            0.606
          ],
          "content": "(b) When the digital root of a number is 9, then the remainder obtained after division by 9 is 0 and if the digital root is less than 9, then the remainder obtained after division by 9 is same as the digital root of that number."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.615,
            0.287,
            0.634
          ],
          "content": "**Page No. 131**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.65,
            0.504,
            0.672
          ],
          "content": "Solve the cryptarithms given below."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.221,
            0.675,
            0.748,
            0.751
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{array}{ccc}& \\text {  1  } & \\\\(i) \\begin{array}{c}\\underline{\\text { A1 }} \\\\\\underline{\\text { + 1B }} \\\\\\underline{\\text { - 1B }}\\end{array} &( ii ) \\begin{array}{c}\\text { AB } \\\\\\underline{\\text { + 37 }} \\\\\\underline{\\text { 6A }}\\end{array} &( iii ) \\begin{array}{c}\\text { ON } \\\\\\underline{\\text { ON }} \\\\\\underline{\\text { ON }} \\\\\\underline{\\text { PQ }}\\end{array} &( iv ) \\begin{array}{c}\\text { QR } \\\\\\text { QR } \\\\\\underline{\\text { + QR }}\\end{array} \\\\\\end{array}",
          "image_source": "images/page_30_equation_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.748,
            0.205,
            0.765
          ],
          "content": "**Ans.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.771,
            0.37,
            0.791
          ],
          "content": "(i) $A = 7, B = 9$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.794,
            0.371,
            0.814
          ],
          "content": "(ii) $A = 2,   B = 5$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.201,
            0.818,
            0.428,
            0.838
          ],
          "content": "(iii) $N = 1,   0 = 3,   \\mathrm{P} = 9$"
        },
        {
